{
  "//": "THE SIDECAR'S TEST DIRECTORY, TYPECHECKED. `tsconfig.json` here covers `src` only and `tsc -b` follows references, so nothing in the workspace ever compiled `apps/sidecar/test/*` — a type error there is invisible to `pnpm typecheck` and the suite runs it anyway, because vitest transpiles without checking. That is how a test file can carry TS2416/TS2554 and stay green (measured in packages/client-engine, 2026-09-06). Run it through the ratchet, never bare: `pnpm -C apps/sidecar run typecheck:tests`.",

  "//paths": "THE ALIASES ARE THE ROOT VITEST TABLE, AND THEY ARE NOT DECORATION. Without them `@trafficflow/core` resolves through node_modules to `packages/core/dist/*.d.ts` — the BUILT declarations — so this config would typecheck the tests against whatever was last compiled rather than against the source vitest actually runs. A stale `dist` would then hide exactly the errors this file exists to find, and a fresh one would report errors nobody can act on. `scripts/typecheck-tests.mjs` imports `vitest.config.ts` and refuses to run if a single `find` in that table has no key here, or if a key points at a different file: the completeness check reads the real alias array, never a regex over the config's text.",

  "//client-engine-durable": "THE DURABLE-WRITE DOOR IS A LEAF, AND IT SITS ABOVE THE BARE NAME. `@ohmail/client-engine/durable` is the fifth hand-written resolver for that specifier; the four before it learned it and this one did not, so `pnpm -C apps/sidecar run typecheck:tests` refused with rc 2 on main for a day — a configuration refusal is a gate saying nothing. The order is the same rule the core subpaths follow: in the vitest table a string `find` is a prefix match, so the barrel placed first rewrites the leaf to `…/src/index.ts/durable` and resolves nothing. `test/durable-write-census.test.ts` now asserts this file by name, entry and order.",

  "//composite": "`false`, overriding the base. A composite project may not disable emit (TS6304), and this program emits nothing.",
  "//jsx": "`react-jsx`, matching packages/ui and apps/desktop, whose files reach this program through imports. Without it every reachable `.tsx` fails with TS6142 and its types never load, so the modules downstream degrade and report errors that are artifacts of the missing setting rather than real ones \u2014 63 of them, including two TS7053 in the shared shell that vanish once the React graph resolves. apps/webapp sets `preserve` instead; that difference is emit only, and this program emits nothing.",

  "//exclude": "node_modules and nothing else. Anything else excluded here is a file that silently stops being checked.",

